Description: Expand a variable used as command name
 With `set $ex exec`, a config line `$ex foo` is accepted but foo never
 runs, while i3 runs it. config_command() replaces a variable in the
 command name, but exec returns CMD_DEFER while the config is loading,
 and read_config() queues the line as written. run_deferred_commands()
 passes it to execute_command(), which only replaces variables in the
 arguments, so it fails with "Unknown/invalid command '$ex'".
 .
 Replace a variable in the command name in execute_command() as well,
 as config_command() does.
Author: rego-port-bot <339843353+rego-port-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Bug: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/issues/7718
Forwarded: https://github.com/swaywm/sway/pull/9326
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
---
diff --git a/sway/commands.c b/sway/commands.c
--- a/sway/commands.c
+++ b/sway/commands.c
